{"id":"cb69b4d43646f13c812d410cc15fc908f5f122c73ae7a5eeea5b88c123dfe196","lamport":0,"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-10-04T12:18:03.132071Z","format_version":1,"kind":"create","payload":{"fields":{"created-at":"2026-10-04T12:18:03.132071Z","created-by":"carlo.cifarelli@gmail.com","description":"Low-risk de-risking step 3/6 of the op-log roadmap (parent 0e7b1245).\n\nReaders safely skip unknown operation types / entity namespaces, so new op kinds\ncan be added by newer clients without breaking older readers (git-bug precedent).\nDe-risks every future op-log change.","parent":"0e7b1245-e860-4843-9df3-101cd9a0a746","priority":"3","spec":"# Spec — Forward-compatible ops (skip unknown op types)\n\nRoadmap step 3/6 (parent 0e7b12). Low-risk; de-risks every future op-log change.\n\n## Goal\n\nGuarantee that a reader encountering an operation type (or entity namespace, or\nfield) it does not understand skips it safely and keeps going, instead of\nerroring or corrupting state. This lets newer clients introduce new op kinds\nwhile older clients still interoperate on the shared op-log.\n\n## Current state (precedent already exists)\n\n- `store.rs::build_ticket` already tolerates unknown scalar fields: its `match`\n  on `(field, value)` has no hard-error catch-all — unrecognized `field` names\n  simply fall through and are ignored. Reads never fail on an unexpected field.\n- This step makes that tolerance an explicit, tested contract and extends it to\n  the operation layer introduced in step 4.\n\n## Design\n\n- Every op carries an explicit `kind` discriminant and a `format-version`\n  (step 2). Deserialization is two-phase: parse the envelope (id, kind, lamport,\n  author, version) first; only then attempt to decode the kind-specific payload.\n- Unknown `kind`: the op is retained verbatim in the log (it still syncs and must\n  not be dropped — dropping would corrupt other clients' replay) but contributes\n  nothing to this binary's derived state. Log a debug line, not an error.\n- Known `kind`, unknown extra payload fields: ignore the extras (serde\n  `#[serde(flatten)]` capture or `deny_unknown_fields` deliberately OFF), so a\n  v-next field is preserved on re-serialize where feasible.\n- Replay is total: an unknown op advances the Lamport position but is a no-op for\n  state folding. `ti verify` (step 4) must treat unknown ops as \"skipped\", not\n  \"drift\".\n\n## Changes\n\n- `oplog` module: `Op` envelope type with `kind: String` + opaque\n  `payload: serde_json::Value`; typed decode attempted per known kind.\n- Tests asserting round-trip preservation of unknown ops and no-panic replay.\n- Document the contract in `keys.rs`/module docs alongside the op key layout.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Unit test: a log containing a synthetic unknown-kind op replays without error\n  and yields the same state as a log without it.\n- Unit test: unknown op survives a read→write→read round-trip (not silently\n  dropped from the synced log).\n- Regression: confirm `build_ticket` still ignores unknown scalar fields.\n\n## Risks\n\n- \"Preserve on re-serialize\" is only fully achievable once writes go through the\n  op-log (step 4); until then, forward-compat is read-side only. Acceptable — the\n  log is append-only, so old clients never rewrite unknown ops anyway.","state":"review","status":"open","title":"Forward-compatible ops (skip unknown op types)"}}}